{"duration_api_ms":48162,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"106e614b-2d96-4af2-9b72-778a7d527a28","total_cost_usd":0.1332458,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19923,"cache_read_input_tokens":3929,"output_tokens":4112,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1859},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19923,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4112,"cache_read_input_tokens":3929,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19923,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19923},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":11569,"outputTokens":15,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.011644,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":4112,"cacheReadInputTokens":3929,"cacheCreationInputTokens":19923,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.12160180000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1859,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"evidence\":[{\"source\":\"node1 log tail, 13:45:25\",\"finding\":\"Group view formed with only 2 members (node1, node2) — node3 absent from this Primary Component.\"},{\"source\":\"node1 log tail, 13:46:51 and 13:53:44\",\"finding\":\"Multiple distinct new group UUIDs appear across successive restarts (01099079-..., fb1ed012-..., 50a0aaa7-...), each reporting members(2) only — indicates repeated re-formation of a 2-node primary component rather than one stable 3-node cluster.\"},{\"source\":\"node2/node3 SST joiner logs, 13:42:37 and 13:42:57\",\"finding\":\"Both node2 and node3 independently entered joiner state requiring full rsync SST ('state transfer needed: yes', Local state 00000000-...:-1), i.e. neither could do incremental state transfer (IST) — they were being treated as if they had no valid prior state.\"},{\"source\":\"node2 command execution, 13:39:31 and 13:45:05\",\"finding\":\"Executor issued pkill -f mysqld_safe / pkill -f mariadbd and later kill -9 on maria/rsync processes — abrupt process kills rather than clean shutdown (e.g. systemctl stop / mysqladmin shutdown).\"},{\"source\":\"node2 filesystem check, 13:56:10 (last record before lease expiry)\",\"finding\":\"/var/lib/mysql still contains rsync_sst.conf, rsync_sst.pid, and sst_in_progress, but `ss -tn` shows no established connection on port 4444 — an SST session appears stale/orphaned at the moment the lease expired, with no confirmation it ever completed.\"},{\"source\":\"Audit summary\",\"finding\":\"160 commands completed with no executor structured report returned, and the run was terminated by cluster_expired at 13:56:17 — the executor never reached a captured state showing wsrep_cluster_size=3 / Synced on all three nodes.\"},{\"source\":\"grep for SST/IST markers, node1 13:47:23\",\"finding\":\"grep for 'IST' and 'Bypassing' in /var/log/messages returned no output (return_code 1 / not found), consistent with the cluster never achieving a clean incremental-state-transfer rejoin path.\"}],\"likely_causes\":[{\"cause\":\"Nodes were restarted without a controlled bootstrap sequence (one designated node first with --wsrep-new-cluster, others joining sequentially afterward and confirmed Synced before the next). Instead multiple nodes appear to have raced into forming independent Primary Components, causing repeated re-election and merge cycles (evidence: 3+ distinct group UUIDs, each with only 2 members).\",\"confidence\":\"high\"},{\"cause\":\"Abrupt process kills (pkill -9 on mariadbd/rsync) during a restart/SST attempt left the datadir in an inconsistent state (grastate.dat with seqno -1, or stale rsync_sst.* artifacts), forcing subsequent joiners into full-SST-required state rather than a fast IST, and possibly causing later SST attempts to stall against leftover lock/pid files.\",\"confidence\":\"medium\"},{\"cause\":\"node3 never durably joined the primary component — all captured post-restart views show only 2 members (node1+node2); node3 may have been stuck retrying a hung rsync SST or blocked on connectivity (port 4444/4567) at the time the lease expired.\",\"confidence\":\"medium\"},{\"cause\":\"Time budget exhaustion: repeated full-SST cycles (each requiring copying the entire datadir via rsync) combined with manual kill/retry loops consumed the cluster lease before a stable 3/3 Synced state was ever reached and verified.\",\"confidence\":\"medium\"}],\"next_attempt_guidance\":[\"Perform a clean, sequenced shutdown: stop mariadb with systemctl stop mariadb (or mysqladmin shutdown) on all three nodes, not pkill/kill -9, so grastate.dat correctly records the last committed seqno and safe_to_bootstrap flag.\",\"Before restarting, inspect grastate.dat on all three nodes and identify the one with the highest seqno (or explicitly set safe_to_bootstrap: 1 on that node) — bootstrap the cluster from that node only, using `galera_new_cluster` or `mariadbd --wsrep-new-cluster`.\",\"Start the remaining two nodes one at a time, waiting for each to report wsrep_local_state_comment = Synced and wsrep_cluster_size incrementing correctly before starting the next node — do not start all three in parallel.\",\"If a node must do SST, let it complete or fail on its own; avoid killing mariadbd/rsync mid-transfer. If a previous SST was interrupted, clean stale artifacts (sst_in_progress, rsync_sst.pid, rsync_sst.conf) from the datadir before retrying, or wipe the joiner's datadir entirely to force a guaranteed-clean full SST.\",\"Before initiating restarts, verify network reachability between all three nodes on the Galera ports (4567 for group comm, 4568 for IST, 4444 for rsync SST) with ss/tcpdump, since SST stalls with no established :4444 connection were observed.\",\"Only declare the maintenance complete after confirming, on all three nodes independently, `SHOW STATUS LIKE 'wsrep_cluster_size'` = 3 and `wsrep_local_state_comment` = Synced, and after spot-checking that a write committed before shutdown is present on each node.\"],\"summary\":\"The attempt never reached a verified 3-node Synced cluster before the lease expired. Log evidence shows repeated restart cycles in which the Primary Component re-formed with only 2 members (node1+node2) under several different group UUIDs, while node2/node3 repeatedly entered joiner state requiring a full rsync SST rather than a fast IST — consistent with restarts that were not sequenced (no single bootstrap node) and with abrupt kill -9 termination of mariadbd/rsync mid-SST. The final captured state on node2, seconds before lease expiry, shows SST artifacts (sst_in_progress, rsync_sst.pid/conf) present but no active rsync connection on port 4444, i.e. a stalled/orphaned state transfer with no confirmation the cluster ever reached wsrep_cluster_size=3.</summary>\\n\"}","structured_output":{"evidence":[{"source":"node1 log tail, 13:45:25","finding":"Group view formed with only 2 members (node1, node2) — node3 absent from this Primary Component."},{"source":"node1 log tail, 13:46:51 and 13:53:44","finding":"Multiple distinct new group UUIDs appear across successive restarts (01099079-..., fb1ed012-..., 50a0aaa7-...), each reporting members(2) only — indicates repeated re-formation of a 2-node primary component rather than one stable 3-node cluster."},{"source":"node2/node3 SST joiner logs, 13:42:37 and 13:42:57","finding":"Both node2 and node3 independently entered joiner state requiring full rsync SST ('state transfer needed: yes', Local state 00000000-...:-1), i.e. neither could do incremental state transfer (IST) — they were being treated as if they had no valid prior state."},{"source":"node2 command execution, 13:39:31 and 13:45:05","finding":"Executor issued pkill -f mysqld_safe / pkill -f mariadbd and later kill -9 on maria/rsync processes — abrupt process kills rather than clean shutdown (e.g. systemctl stop / mysqladmin shutdown)."},{"source":"node2 filesystem check, 13:56:10 (last record before lease expiry)","finding":"/var/lib/mysql still contains rsync_sst.conf, rsync_sst.pid, and sst_in_progress, but `ss -tn` shows no established connection on port 4444 — an SST session appears stale/orphaned at the moment the lease expired, with no confirmation it ever completed."},{"source":"Audit summary","finding":"160 commands completed with no executor structured report returned, and the run was terminated by cluster_expired at 13:56:17 — the executor never reached a captured state showing wsrep_cluster_size=3 / Synced on all three nodes."},{"source":"grep for SST/IST markers, node1 13:47:23","finding":"grep for 'IST' and 'Bypassing' in /var/log/messages returned no output (return_code 1 / not found), consistent with the cluster never achieving a clean incremental-state-transfer rejoin path."}],"likely_causes":[{"cause":"Nodes were restarted without a controlled bootstrap sequence (one designated node first with --wsrep-new-cluster, others joining sequentially afterward and confirmed Synced before the next). Instead multiple nodes appear to have raced into forming independent Primary Components, causing repeated re-election and merge cycles (evidence: 3+ distinct group UUIDs, each with only 2 members).","confidence":"high"},{"cause":"Abrupt process kills (pkill -9 on mariadbd/rsync) during a restart/SST attempt left the datadir in an inconsistent state (grastate.dat with seqno -1, or stale rsync_sst.* artifacts), forcing subsequent joiners into full-SST-required state rather than a fast IST, and possibly causing later SST attempts to stall against leftover lock/pid files.","confidence":"medium"},{"cause":"node3 never durably joined the primary component — all captured post-restart views show only 2 members (node1+node2); node3 may have been stuck retrying a hung rsync SST or blocked on connectivity (port 4444/4567) at the time the lease expired.","confidence":"medium"},{"cause":"Time budget exhaustion: repeated full-SST cycles (each requiring copying the entire datadir via rsync) combined with manual kill/retry loops consumed the cluster lease before a stable 3/3 Synced state was ever reached and verified.","confidence":"medium"}],"next_attempt_guidance":["Perform a clean, sequenced shutdown: stop mariadb with systemctl stop mariadb (or mysqladmin shutdown) on all three nodes, not pkill/kill -9, so grastate.dat correctly records the last committed seqno and safe_to_bootstrap flag.","Before restarting, inspect grastate.dat on all three nodes and identify the one with the highest seqno (or explicitly set safe_to_bootstrap: 1 on that node) — bootstrap the cluster from that node only, using `galera_new_cluster` or `mariadbd --wsrep-new-cluster`.","Start the remaining two nodes one at a time, waiting for each to report wsrep_local_state_comment = Synced and wsrep_cluster_size incrementing correctly before starting the next node — do not start all three in parallel.","If a node must do SST, let it complete or fail on its own; avoid killing mariadbd/rsync mid-transfer. If a previous SST was interrupted, clean stale artifacts (sst_in_progress, rsync_sst.pid, rsync_sst.conf) from the datadir before retrying, or wipe the joiner's datadir entirely to force a guaranteed-clean full SST.","Before initiating restarts, verify network reachability between all three nodes on the Galera ports (4567 for group comm, 4568 for IST, 4444 for rsync SST) with ss/tcpdump, since SST stalls with no established :4444 connection were observed.","Only declare the maintenance complete after confirming, on all three nodes independently, `SHOW STATUS LIKE 'wsrep_cluster_size'` = 3 and `wsrep_local_state_comment` = Synced, and after spot-checking that a write committed before shutdown is present on each node."],"summary":"The attempt never reached a verified 3-node Synced cluster before the lease expired. Log evidence shows repeated restart cycles in which the Primary Component re-formed with only 2 members (node1+node2) under several different group UUIDs, while node2/node3 repeatedly entered joiner state requiring a full rsync SST rather than a fast IST — consistent with restarts that were not sequenced (no single bootstrap node) and with abrupt kill -9 termination of mariadbd/rsync mid-SST. The final captured state on node2, seconds before lease expiry, shows SST artifacts (sst_in_progress, rsync_sst.pid/conf) present but no active rsync connection on port 4444, i.e. a stalled/orphaned state transfer with no confirmation the cluster ever reached wsrep_cluster_size=3.</summary>\n"},"ttft_ms":24943,"type":"result","duration_ms":46932,"uuid":"02678f47-fe1e-4e6c-898b-26356cfcdfd3","ttft_stream_ms":2516,"time_to_request_ms":37,"first_content_frame_ms":3074,"queued_turn_count":0}
